Task 6: K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN) Classification 

Project Goal
To understand and implement K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN), an instance-based, non-parametric model, focusing on the critical role of feature scaling and the selection of the optimal 'K' value.

Key Outcomes & Skills
a. Non-Parametric Implementation: Successfully implemented the KNeighbors Classifier from Scikit-learn, demonstrating a grasp of how this algorithm classifies data points based on Euclidean distance from its neighbors.
b. Feature Scaling Requirement: Applied feature normalization/scaling to the dataset, recognizing its essential role in KNN to prevent distance calculations from being dominated by features with larger magnitudes.
c. Optimal K Selection: Developed a methodical approach to experiment with different values of K, using model performance (accuracy) to determine the optimal number of neighbors for generalization.
d. Evaluation & Visualization: Evaluated model performance using standard metrics (Accuracy, Confusion Matrix) and visualized the model's decision boundaries to illustrate the classification process.

Tools and Techniques
    | Category                | Technique/Concept                                                                                           | 
    | :-----------------------| :---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------: | 
    | Libraries               | Scikit-learn (KNeighborsClassifier), Pandas, Matplotlib.                                                                     |
    | Concepts                | Instance-Based Learning, Euclidean Distance, K Selection, Feature Normalization, Decision Boundaries.  | 
    | Dataset Used            | Iris Dataset.                                                                                      | 
    
